    {
      "id": "6e1abvw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Distinction between noun and verb forms is vital for word pairs like Advice vs Advise and Practice vs Practise.",
        "Affect is predominantly used as a verb meaning 'to influence', whereas Effect is usually a noun meaning 'a result'.",
        "Prepositions like Beside (by the side of) and Besides (in addition to) carry vastly different meanings.",
        "Verbs such as Borrow (receive temporarily) and Lend (give temporarily) denote opposite directions of transaction.",
        "Differentiating similar-sounding or visually similar words is essential for solving error detection questions in competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "bk5vtye"
    },
